{
    "version": "https://jsonfeed.org/version/1",
    "title": "mdn/browser-compat-data update data",
    "home_page_url": "https://azu.github.io/github-search-rss/mdn-browser-compat-data.json",
    "feed_url": "https://azu.github.io/github-search-rss/mdn-browser-compat-data.json",
    "description": "mdn/browser-compat-data update data on GitHub",
    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 149 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSPseudoElement</code> interface and <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.pseudo()</code> method; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194399398756352\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194399398756352</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": true</code> to the main interface, with a note to say that it doesn't inherit from <code class=\"notranslate\">EventTarget</code>, like the spec says it should. I've tested it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also wanted to bring up that, in my local MDN, the BCD support tables for this interface are generated, but the spec tables are not. This doesn't make sense, as the <code class=\"notranslate\">spec_url</code> fields are included.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29792",
            "title": "Add partial and note to CSSPseudoElement",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T10:33:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-02T10:09:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33368817?u=80d39153e27b7d191281ed9b12cfb2b414418080&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Problem</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470059571\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44167\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44167/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44167\">mdn/content#44167</a> tracks Firefox 152 Nightly support for WebAssembly JavaScript Promise Integration (JS-PI), but BCD still marked Firefox as unsupported.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Root cause</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">webassembly/jspi.json</code> had no Firefox support entry for the new Nightly implementation.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Solution</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mark Firefox 152 support behind the <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.options.wasm_js_promise_integration</code> preference. Firefox for Android continues to mirror desktop Firefox for this feature.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Tests run</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">node lint/lint.js webassembly/jspi.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">node_modules/.bin/prettier.cmd --check webassembly/jspi.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('webassembly/jspi.json','utf8')); console.log('ok')\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29783",
            "title": "Update Firefox support for WebAssembly JS-PI",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T09:33:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-01T18:01:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "KirtiRamchandani",
                "url": "https://github.com/KirtiRamchandani"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33368817?u=80d39153e27b7d191281ed9b12cfb2b414418080&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Problem</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 152 enables the Crash Reporting API in Nightly builds via <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.reporting.crash.enabled</code>, but BCD still listed the CrashReportContext storage APIs as unsupported in Firefox.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Root cause</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Gecko change only flips the Crash Reporting API preference for Nightly builds, so the existing Chromium-only data needed Firefox support entries behind that preference.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Solution</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update Firefox support for:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.CrashReportContext</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.CrashReportContext.delete</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.CrashReportContext.initialize</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.CrashReportContext.set</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Window.crashReport</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Each entry is marked as added in Firefox 152 behind <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.reporting.crash.enabled</code>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Tests</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --yes npm@11.12.1 --prefix C:\\Users\\kirti\\Documents\\PRs\\browser-compat-data run lint -- api/CrashReportContext.json api/Window.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">C:\\Users\\kirti\\Documents\\PRs\\browser-compat-data\\node_modules\\.bin\\prettier.cmd --check C:\\Users\\kirti\\Documents\\PRs\\browser-compat-data\\api\\CrashReportContext.json C:\\Users\\kirti\\Documents\\PRs\\browser-compat-data\\api\\Window.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">node -e \"const fs=require('fs'); for (const f of ['C:/Users/kirti/Documents/PRs/browser-compat-data/api/CrashReportContext.json','C:/Users/kirti/Documents/PRs/browser-compat-data/api/Window.json']) JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8')); console.log('JSON OK')\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">References</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4548448348\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44297\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44297/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44297\">mdn/content#44297</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2036160\" rel=\"nofollow\">Firefox bug 2036160</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29782",
            "title": "Update Firefox support for Crash Reporting API",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T10:03:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-01T16:41:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "KirtiRamchandani",
                "url": "https://github.com/KirtiRamchandani"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33368817?u=80d39153e27b7d191281ed9b12cfb2b414418080&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update Firefox compatibility data for <code class=\"notranslate\">appearance: base-select</code> and the single-dropdown customizable select subfeature.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox bug 1974787 was fixed for Firefox 149 and added <code class=\"notranslate\">appearance: base-select</code> behind <code class=\"notranslate\">layout.css.appearance-base-select.enabled</code>. This updates the general <code class=\"notranslate\">base-select</code> value and the single-dropdown subfeature with the corresponding preference flag.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I left the listbox and multiple-dropdown subfeatures unchanged because the Firefox bug documents the customizable <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;select&gt;</code> value, but does not establish those separate subfeatures.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Tests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npm run lint -- css/properties/appearance.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">prettier --check css/properties/appearance.json</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('css/properties/appearance.json','utf8')); console.log('valid json')\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1974787\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1974787</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4562221013\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44320\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/44320/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44320\">mdn/content#44320</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29780",
            "title": "Update Firefox data for appearance: base-select",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T09:34:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-01T10:19:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "KirtiRamchandani",
                "url": "https://github.com/KirtiRamchandani"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update to reflect that <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2034168\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2034168</a> including a change so that<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">extension.isAllowedFileSchemeAccess()</code> reflects the value of the \"Access local files on your computer\" option in the extension's permissions settings.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Four related content changes see PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4565226252\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44328\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/44328/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44328\">mdn/content#44328</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29776",
            "title": "Bug 2034168 extension.isAllowedFileSchemeAccess reflects file access permission",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-01T18:04:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-31T23:33:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 148 adds support for name-only container queries; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184267522015232\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184267522015232</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> BCD file already has a data point about name-only container queries, but I thought it would be a good idea to add data points about this to the <code class=\"notranslate\">container-name</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">container-type</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">container</code> property BCD. Those pages will include examples/information about name-only queries, and I think they are common places where people will want this compat info.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29762",
            "title": "Add data points about name-only container queries",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T11:02:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-27T16:48:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for importing text modules in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854</a> (this uses the <code class=\"notranslate\">with</code> clause <code class=\"notranslate\">{type: \"text\"}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the text type subfeature, and corresponding <code class=\"notranslate\">text</code> destination for fetch requests. This doesn't seem to be supported in Chrome or Safari (quick search). I've set other platforms to false, except for BUN</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470056163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44166/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\">mdn/content#44166</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29745",
            "title": "FF152 with clause {type: \"text\"}",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-02T10:52:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T02:57:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 adds support for the <a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#dom-speechrecognitionoptions-quality\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">SpeechRecognitionOptions</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code> property</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object overall, and then a subdata point for <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code>, for both methods that use this <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object — <code class=\"notranslate\">available()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">install()</code>. I am not 100% sure about this structure, but I copied it from </p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json#L229\">browser-compat-data/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n         Line 229\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/commit/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c\">c077200</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L229\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"229\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC229\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-ent\">\"options_parameter\"</span>: { </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n.<p></p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29741",
